Just now I was looking back through my folder of completed patches, and
I noticed that one of them hadn't been officially released by me yet,
even though it's been complete for months. So, here it is:

< http://www.greyfire.org/~l/aleax.diff >

Currently Aleaxes are just another variety of angel, and the only kind
which can't fly, at that. This patch makes them more closely resemble
their AD&D counterparts.

* Aleaxes only appear through your god's wrath.
* When your own god sends a hostile monster, it will always be an
Aleax.
* If you have negative alignment, further alignment penalties have a
chance of summoning an Aleax.
* Aleaxes are created with exact copies (barring artifacts) of your
wielded weapons and armor (provided they are actual weapons.)
Considering that you need to transgress your alignment to summon one,
and also that you need to defeat the Aleax to acquire its equipment, I
don't think this is very abusive.

Also, some tweaks to various alignment bonuses:
* Fixed a 'bug' where lawfuls can increase their alignment by
repeatedly attempting to genocide a demon.
* Fixed a 'bug' where all chaotic characters _except_ chaotic rogues
get an alignment bonus for stealing from shops.
* Fixed some areas where chaotic archeologists, samurai or knights got
alignment changes.
* Committing murder now 'tells you' that your intrinsic telepathy was
removed.
* Converting an altar adds 2 to a priest's alignment.



